<title>BELGIUM: Cockerill to skip dividend.</title>
<headline>Cockerill to skip dividend.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belgian steel group Cockerill Sambre said on Wednesday it would pay no dividend on 1996 earnings.</p>
<p>Last year the group paid a gross dividend of 25.6 francs per preferred share.  </p>
<p>Cockerill chairman Jean Gandois told a news conference &quot;there will not be a dividend, having made a nine billion franc loss.&quot;</p>
<p>&quot;If there is a little profit in 1997, there will be a dividend, though perhaps not a full one,&quot; he added.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
